title: Instructions/rename_tiddler

Renames a tiddler in the store and moves its file on disk to the path `FileSystemPaths` gives the new title. The operation fails if the new title clashes with an existing tiddler, unless `overwrite` is `true`. Bundled plugin, theme and language tiddlers and `.multids` entries are refused.

|!Parameter |!Required |!Description |
|`from` |yes |Existing tiddler title |
|`to` |yes |New tiddler title |
|`overwrite` |no |Set to `true` to replace an existing tiddler at `to` (default: `false`) |
|`preserve_timestamps` |no |Keep the original `modified` field (default: `true`). Set `false` to set it to now |

''Behaviour:''

* All fields are preserved, `modified` included; set `preserve_timestamps=false` to refresh `modified` and `modifier`.
* The old `.tid` file is deleted after the new file is written successfully (with verification re-read).
* Cross-references in other tiddlers are NOT updated — use `replace_in_tiddlers` to follow up (see [[Rename references across the wiki]]).

> ''Note:'' This is a single-tiddler rename; for bulk find-and-replace across the wiki, see [[Bulk Tools]].

''Example prompts:''

* "Rename the tiddler OldName to NewName"
* "Rename HelloThere to Welcome"
